---
import Layout from '@layouts/Layout.astro';
import AdSlot from '@components/AdSlot.astro';
---

<Layout
  lang="en"
  title="Palworld Tech Tree Guide - 588 Techs + Priority List"
  description="Palworld tech tree complete guide. 588 techs grouped by unlock level (Lv 1-80), marked must-get / recommended / skip. The 1.0 endgame techs and the full upgrade route, 1-hour read."
>
  <article class="guide-content">
    <header class="page-header">
      <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/en/guides/">Guides</a> › Tech Tree</p>
      <h1>🔬 Palworld Tech Tree: Must-Get / Recommended / Skip</h1>
      <p class="text-secondary">588 techs · unlock levels Lv 1-80 · Palworld 1.0 + DLCs + Sunreach + World Tree</p>
    </header>

    <AdSlot position="inline" />

    <section>
      <h2>How the Tech Tree Works: Level + Materials</h2>
      <p>
        Palworld has <strong>588 techs</strong> split into <strong>Structures</strong> and <strong>Items</strong>.
        Each tech requires an <strong>unlock level</strong> (the cap is <strong>Lv 80</strong> as of 1.0), <strong>Ancient Technology Points</strong> and <strong>materials</strong>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Ancient Technology Points come from: killing bosses, opening map chests, and catching certain Pals.
        Early game, Penking is the best farm - it gives 3-5 points per kill.
      </p>
    </section>

    <AdSlot position="inline" />

    <section>
      <h2>Must-Get: Levels 1-10 (10 Techs You Cannot Skip)</h2>
      <p>These 10 techs are the foundation of the early game. Skipping any of them makes life painful:</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Primitive Workbench - tools and Spheres</li>
        <li>Palbox - store Pals, swap team</li>
        <li>Global Palbox (Lv 7) - fast travel between bases</li>
        <li>Wooden Structure Set - basic building</li>
        <li>Ranch - breeding</li>
        <li><a href="/en/tech-tree/Special_PalSphere_Grade_01/">Pal Sphere</a> series - upgrade to Mega Sphere</li>
        <li>Repair Bench - fix gear</li>
        <li>Campfire - cooking</li>
        <li>Straw Pal Bed - Pal sleep recovery</li>
        <li>Pal Dressing Facility - Pal skins, stat boosts</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <AdSlot position="inline" />

    <section>
      <h2>Recommended: Levels 11-20 Key Upgrades</h2>
      <p>Mid-game essentials that affect combat and progression speed:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Cloth series</strong>: <a href="/en/tech-tree/Battle_Cloth/">Cloth Outfit</a> - upgrade leather to cloth armor</li>
        <li><strong>Metal tools</strong>: <a href="/en/tech-tree/Product_Factory_Hard_Grade_01/">Improved Workbench</a> + iron pickaxe, 2x mining speed</li>
        <li><strong>Sphere upgrades</strong>: Giga Sphere series, needed for high-rarity catches</li>
        <li><strong>Weapon Bench</strong>: <a href="/en/tech-tree/Product_WeaponFactory_Dirty_Grade_01/">Weapon Workbench II</a> - muskets and bows</li>
        <li><strong>Large Palbox</strong>: <a href="/en/tech-tree/PALBOX/">Large Palbox</a> - 60 Pal storage</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <AdSlot position="inline" />

    <section>
      <h2>Skip: Techs You Can Postpone</h2>
      <p>Unless you specifically need them, these can wait:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Furniture Sets</strong>: pure decoration, the furniture series can wait</li>
        <li><strong>Vehicle upgrades</strong>: advanced glider fuel, not needed until late game</li>
        <li><strong>Advanced clothes</strong>: <a href="/en/tech-tree/Battle_Armor_Grade_01_Cloth_Cold/">Cold Outfit</a> and similar, wait until you reach Sakurajima</li>
        <li><strong>Neon lights / signs</strong>: pure decoration</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <AdSlot position="inline" />

    <section>
      <h2>Tech Tree Upgrade Route: Lv 1-80</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Lv 1-7</strong>: must-get 10 techs, lay the foundation</li>
        <li><strong>Lv 8-15</strong>: Cloth Outfit + Weapon Workbench II + breeding techs</li>
        <li><strong>Lv 16-25</strong>: Giga Sphere upgrade + Cold Outfit prep for Sakurajima</li>
        <li><strong>Lv 26-40</strong>: Metal Armor + Advanced Weapon, ready for boss fights</li>
        <li><strong>Lv 41-50</strong>: Feybreak entry kit, neon furniture sets</li>
        <li><strong>Lv 51-65</strong>: Hexolite material line + laser weapons, gearing up for towers 5-6</li>
        <li><strong>Lv 66-70</strong>: Soralite sky weapons + the Azure Covenant tower boss (Lv 68)</li>
        <li><strong>Lv 71-80</strong>: Ancient Series + Paloxite, gearing up for the final tower boss Zenara &amp; Astralym</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        Want to check what materials each tech needs? Visit the <a href="/en/tech-tree/">full Tech Tree</a>
        with all 588 techs, descriptions, materials, and real unlock levels (Lv 1-80).
      </p>
    </section>

    <AdSlot position="inline" />

    <section>
      <h2>Lv 51-80: The 1.0 Endgame Tech List</h2>
      <p>With the cap at 80, the endgame techs unlock in three stages. These are the must-gets:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Lv 51-60 · Hexolite and heavy ranged weapons</strong>:
          <a href="/en/tech-tree/StainlessSteel/">Hexolite</a> (Lv 58),
          <a href="/en/tech-tree/SFArmor/">Hexolite Armor</a> (Lv 59),
          <a href="/en/tech-tree/LaserGatlingGun/">Laser Gatling Gun</a> (Lv 59),
          <a href="/en/tech-tree/EnergyRocketLauncher/">Plasma Cannon</a> (Lv 61)
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Lv 61-70 · Sunreach and the sky series</strong>:
          <a href="/en/tech-tree/SkyislandIngot/">Soralite Ingot</a> (Lv 66),
          <a href="/en/tech-tree/SkyBow/">Mechanical Bow</a> (Lv 67),
          <a href="/en/tech-tree/SkyIslandOrePit/">Soralite Quarry</a> (Lv 72),
          <a href="/en/tech-tree/Accessory_JumpCount_Increase2/">Triple Jump Boots</a> (Lv 70)
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Lv 71-80 · the Ancient Series</strong>:
          <a href="/en/tech-tree/AncientArmor/">Ancient Armor</a> (Lv 68),
          <a href="/en/tech-tree/AncientHelmet/">Ancient Helm</a> (Lv 68),
          <a href="/en/tech-tree/Shield_07/">Ancient Shield</a> (Lv 71),
          <a href="/en/tech-tree/WorldTreeIngot/">Paloxite Ingot</a> (Lv 74),
          <a href="/en/tech-tree/AncientRelicRecycler/">Ancient Relic Recycler</a> (Lv 74),
          <a href="/en/tech-tree/PalSphere_Ancient_2/">Ancient Sphere</a> (Lv 74)
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        These are the hard requirements for the final tower boss Zenara &amp; Astralym (Lv 80).
        For the full 1.0 breakdown see the <a href="/en/guides/palworld-1-0-guide/">Palworld 1.0 complete guide</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <AdSlot position="inline" />

    <section>
      <h2>Ancient Tech Point Farming Tips</h2>
      <p>Ancient Tech Points are the most scarce early resource. The 3 most effective sources:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Kill bosses</strong>: Penking and Kingpaca are easy farms, 3-5 points each</li>
        <li><strong>Map chests</strong>: open all chests within 200m of your <a href="/en/guides/base-building-guide/">base</a></li>
        <li><strong>Catch boss-tier Pals</strong>: rarity 8+ catches give 1-2 points</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="related-links">
      <h2>View Now</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/en/tech-tree/">📊 Full 588 Tech Tree</a></li>
        <li><a href="/en/guides/palworld-1-0-guide/">🆕 Palworld 1.0 Complete Guide</a></li>
        <li><a href="/en/guides/beginner-guide/">🎮 Beginner Guide</a></li>
        <li><a href="/en/guides/base-building-guide/">🏠 Base Building</a></li>
        <li><a href="/en/calculator/power/">⚡ Power Calculator</a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .guide-content { max-width: 820px; margin: 0 auto; line-height: 1.8; }
  .page-header { margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .breadcrumb { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 0.9rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .breadcrumb a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
  h1 { font-size: 2rem; margin: 0.5rem 0; line-height: 1.3; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.5rem; margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem; color: var(--accent); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); padding-left: 0.8rem; }
  p { margin: 0.8rem 0; }
  ul, ol { margin: 0.8rem 0; padding-left: 1.5rem; }
  li { margin: 0.5rem 0; }
  a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: underline; }
  .related-links { margin-top: 3rem; padding: 1.5rem; background: var(--bg-secondary); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); }
  .related-links ul { list-style: none; padding: 0; }
  .related-links li { padding: 0.3rem 0; }
</style>
